# Blender writes one of these beside a file every time it saves over it.
*.blend1

# A crash dumps one of these into the process's working directory, which on a
# checkout is the repository root. The suite crashes harnesses on purpose, so a
# `git add -A` has swept a hundred megabytes of core into a commit before.
/core
core.[0-9]*
